course: dictionary
lesson: 10076
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word thatch can name a roof covering, or describe a thick, messy mass of hair. Context, the words and sentences around the word, tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: In history lessons, thatch was used to cover roofs of old cottages and Iron Age roundhouses. The word «thatched» means roofed, usually with straw. A thatcher is the person who does this job.
explain: When you see a word you know, check it still fits. Is someone covering a roof, or describing hair? Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it makes sense.
fact: Thatch is a roof covering made of straw, reeds or similar dried plants, laid thickly.
fact: To thatch a roof means to cover it with thatch.
fact: A thatcher is a person who thatches roofs.
fact: Thatch keeps rain out because water runs down the steep straw.
fact: Informal: «a thatch of hair» means a thick, untidy mass of hair.
exercise: Thatch keeps rain out because water runs down the steep straw. What keeps the rain out? | A tall chimney | Iron bars | *The steep, thick straw | A plastic sheet
exercise: «Her thatch of hair was messy and thick.» What does thatch mean here? | A type of hat | A small wooden hut | A roof covering | *A thick, untidy mass of hair
exercise: Which word in this list means roofed? «giddy», «by-the-bye», «thatched», «grant» | giddy | by-the-bye | *thatched | grant
test: The workers ______ the barn roof with straw. Which word fits? | thatcher | thatchy | thatches | *thatched
test: What is a thatcher? | *A person who thatches roofs | A person who cuts hair | A farmer who grows straw | A builder of brick walls
exam: «The old cottage had a thatch of straw on its roof.» What does thatch mean here? | A thatcher's tool | *A roof covering made of dried plants | A dried reed used for weaving | A thick, untidy mass of hair
